    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make an easy, 7-minute salmon piccata with capers. This recipe starts by seasoning the salmon fillets with salt, pepper, and cayenne. After sprinkling a dash of flour over the meat, sear them in a skillet with clarified butter. Remove the salmon from the skillet to create a sauce that’s mixed with crushed capers, white wine, and lemon. Once the sauce has thickened, add the salmon back to the pan to finish it off. Unlike other salmon recipes that dry the fish out, this dinner recipe is moist, tender, and practically melts in your mouth.",
